    {
        "content": "<p>I wish this was called something better than <code>repeat'</code>.</p>",
        "id": 609765555,
        "sender_full_name": "François G. Dorais",
        "timestamp": 1783922590
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I thought it'd be better named <code>rconstructor</code> as tiny util. (and more optimize instaed of <code>repeat'</code>)</p>",
        "id": 609765708,
        "sender_full_name": "SnO2WMaN",
        "timestamp": 1783922662
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>in mathlib we have <code>constructorm</code></p>",
        "id": 609774944,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1783927145
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>which in this case allows you to write the more specific <code>constructorm* (_ ∧ _)</code> instead of <code>repeat' constructor</code></p>",
        "id": 609776197,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1783927555
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I didn't know, sound nice!</p>",
        "id": 609805306,
        "sender_full_name": "SnO2WMaN",
        "timestamp": 1783937633
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Isn't this <code>and_intros</code></p>",
        "id": 609808059,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Meiburg",
        "timestamp": 1783938860
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In fact, we have both <code>and_intros</code> and <code>split_ands</code> as tactics that do the same thing! I learned that just now but we've been discussing what to do about this fact for a bit. See also: <a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"113488\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/and_intros.20vs.2E.20split_ands/with/579583990\">#general &gt; and_intros vs. split_ands</a></p>",
        "id": 609845476,
        "sender_full_name": "Anne Baanen",
        "timestamp": 1783951041
    }
